edical tests; evidence should clearly show real correlations. This is especially important in the lesion section.**Exploring Deliberation and Action**\n\nI’m examining how deliberation relates to uncertain action dynamics. The self-prediction problem remains: if an idealized agent knows its deterministic algorithm, some alternatives might hold a probability of zero, which can lead to misleading information. I focus on requiring an explicit positive-support model to account for uncertainties in implementation and reasoning. This is a modeling proposal. It’s essential to clarify that action sets don't create independent stochastic probabilities and that sequential invariance may not hold if evidence changes.**Checking EDT Consistency**\n\nI need to clarify whether EDT can be generally inconsistent in a dynamic context. I should verify the consistency of conditioning with a given policy. Basic EDT might involve maximizing expected utility, but the differences can arise based on sequential choices if events and earlier conditions are partially known. There’s no guarantee that policy rankings will match later rankings, so I must model commitment and revision opportunities. I can conclude that there are no simple assumptions for policy in canonical EDT.","format":"openai-responses-v1","index":6},{"type":"reasoning.encrypted","data":"gAAAAABq8QU9W6h2ISPxgmGHi5VcyrOTBnmB1Oo-_GvxJF3_5gfpKCdYtlKoaiKqmisgn2mMlW-FRtuoVkez00N4x4kTHpAy0FM7pescUZEugsdjk9zv2lCpdEB5eFCfzsGEU92tn21DukS29kl5YwZbUtmoLYiu_7y4TK6zNE_lCOryDEpVAmhZFnET4vQasRGG4ulOQMiPiNsRqC8UCs9d9JXpW_UVgZY16eIZJHavU7t0Vwqwj2N4wnZwpsyMymM5B2YX1nKXGzYw28ZhVwdqJcWMYtlIZEszvJS02JWiqU3j0WFRJkQl9ShFacovCeBomAIwojtmsBYkx3qW0PpyEdF9jCu0WG3URmLDqU5F8DSscEP0Ii8eLP_gHDan_drGpOo74NnmYPO1NnhX4Lu9h8G7UVGRLCGeClAs1XnPC2ZCJN8LFVe_SQ0Kr1WmwerXK_kOdHocBPOpDRpQJy2KTyrLzcpeS9lVv4OJX-M2H269jd7kb9G33EF5JjbpTv56GKyQ6ArrsWQ0wmqTjips32BWNwDRiElZOFdl-3SwU8RpF9iJci4Z2XtmxinbAqV2_cHEwQu9uHbC7KKdhwu90smoDjKdfFTvSaKZOrxGOo5f1q9Ctunx_AlPiwfna0kWQ4v3Fjs